## What the Allocation Does to the Chart

Holding 23% back means the curve has fewer tokens to sell for the same 85 SOL. The honest consequence, stated here rather than discovered on a chart:

| Measure | A launch with no allocation | DESHILL 002 |
|---|---|---|
| Opening market cap | ~27 SOL | **~52 SOL** |
| Graduation market cap | 425 SOL | **425 SOL** |
| Move from open to graduation | ~16x | **~8x** |

DESHILL opens at roughly double the market cap of a launch with no allocation and graduates at the same place, so the move from launch to graduation is about half. Graduation also arrives sooner in token terms, because there is less supply for the curve to sell.

This is the unavoidable trade-off of any allocation. It is the cost of funding an airdrop, and it is disclosed up front.

